@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- National Insurance Law [Consolidated Version], 5755-1995, ss 65-68 (the child allowance).
-- THE NOUNS: DECLARE and nothing else. Every rule module imports this one.
--
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/national-insurance-law-consolidated-version-5755-1995.he.wiki.txt,
-- Hebrew Wikisource raw MediaWiki, retrieved 2026-10-06, sha256 78bf47ee...552a97.
-- An unofficial consolidation of the text as amended at retrieval. A `src:N` comment quotes
-- line N of that file, generated by tools/srcquote.py; nothing in Hebrew here is typed by hand.
--
-- Money is new Israeli shekels (NIS) per month, as a bare NUMBER.
-- Membership test for this module: a witness of ordinary competence could testify to the
-- fact, or a register of the Institute records it. Whether the fact makes a person insured,
-- a child a "child", or an allowance payable is a rule, and belongs in the section module
-- that says so.

§ `Nouns for sections 65 to 68`

§§ `A person who may be a parent`

-- Every fact below is as it stands on the day asked about (`A family on a day`), except the
-- two s 68(c) facts, which are about the month in which that day falls.
--
-- `name`: identity. Two records with one name are one person (phrasebook 6.6); a child's
-- record points at its parents by name.
--
-- `insured under Chapter 11` and `a housewife as defined in section 238`: s 65's two
-- limbs of "insured" turn on them. Chapter 11 is old-age and survivors' insurance; s 238
-- defines "housewife" for it. Both are statuses the Institute records, outside this row.
-- src:801 | ”מבוטח“ –
-- src:802 | (1) מבוטח לפי פרק י״א, למעט עקרת בית כהגדרתה בסעיף 238;
-- src:803 | (2) יחיד היושב בישראל, ואינו נעדר ממנה אלא העדר ארעי שהוא סביר, לדעת עובד המוסד שהוסמך לכך, ואין בו לסתור טענת אותו יחיד כי הוא יושב בישראל, ואינו מבוטח לפי פרק י״א, למעט עקרת בית כהגדרתה בסעיף 238;
--
-- `resident in Israel` and `absent from Israel beyond a reasonable temporary absence`: the
-- second limb of "insured". The second fact is the opinion of the Institute's employee
-- authorised for it, that the person is absent other than for a temporary absence that is
-- reasonable and does not contradict the person's claim to reside in Israel; it is a
-- recorded determination, not something this row decides.
--
-- `formerly insured`: TRUE for a person who was insured and, on the day, has died or is no
-- longer insured. s 65 "ילד" (1) counts the child of "one who was insured"; s 71, which is
-- not encoded, says what is paid by virtue of such a parent.
-- src:805 | (1) ילדו של מבוטח או של מי שהיה מבוטח;
--
-- `income chargeable to additional tax under section 121B of the Income Tax Ordinance`:
-- s 66's exception. Whether income is so chargeable is decided under the Ordinance (row
-- IL-03 encodes s 121B); this row takes the answer as given (fork F5 on which tax year).
-- src:814 | הורה מבוטח זכאי לקצבת ילדים חודשית לפי פרק זה בעד כל ילד, למעט הורה מבוטח שיש לו הכנסה החייבת במס נוסף כמשמעותה בסעיף 121ב לפקודת מס הכנסה.
--
-- `paid, for the month, a benefit under the Income Support Law` and `paid, for the month, a
-- monthly payment under the Maintenance (Assurance of Payment) Law`: the s 68(c) condition.
-- Both are payments the Institute makes and records.
-- src:826 | (ג) הורה שמשתלמים לו בעד חודש מסוים גמלה לפי חוק הבטחת הכנסה או תשלום חודשי לפי חוק המזונות (הבטחת תשלום), התשל״ב–1972, והוא זכאי בעד אותו חודש לקצבת ילדים כאמור בסעיפים קטנים (א) או (ב) בעד שלושה ילדים או יותר, תיווסף לקצבת הילדים המשתלמת לו בעד הילד השלישי ובעד הילד הרביעי שבמנין ילדיו תוספת בסכום השווה ל־70% מן הסכום הבסיסי הקבוע בפסקה (2)(ג) שבהגדרה ”הסכום הבסיסי“.
--
-- `children by more than one woman`: the fact that brings s 69A, which is not encoded, into
-- play for an insured man. "נשים" can be read as women or as wives; the wider reading is
-- taken so that every case s 69A might reach is declined (fork F13).
-- src:843 | על אף האמור בכל מקום אחר בסימן זה, היו למבוטח ילדים ממספר נשים יחולו לגביו הוראות אלה:
DECLARE `A person` HAS
    `name`                                                                                       IS A STRING
    `insured under Chapter 11`                                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `a housewife as defined in section 238`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `resident in Israel`                                                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `absent from Israel beyond a reasonable temporary absence`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `formerly insured`                                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `income chargeable to additional tax under section 121B of the Income Tax Ordinance`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid, for the month, a benefit under the Income Support Law`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid, for the month, a monthly payment under the Maintenance (Assurance of Payment) Law`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `children by more than one woman`                                                            IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `How a person stands to a child`

-- s 65 "ילד" (1) is "the child of an insured" read with s 1, under which "child" includes a
-- stepchild and an adopted child (fork F1). (2) is a child who is NOT the person's child but
-- whom the insured supported. s 67(b)'s second limb turns on "a natural parent".
-- src:170 | ”ילד“ – לרבות ילד חורג וילד מאומץ ולמעט נער ונערה נשואים;
-- src:806 | (2) מי שאינו ילדו, אם הוכח, להנחת דעתו של מי שהסמיכה לכך המינהלה, כי בתקופה שנקבעה בתקנות פירנס אותו המבוטח,
DECLARE `Standing to the child` IS ONE OF
    `the child's natural parent`
    `the child's adoptive parent`
    `the child's step-parent`
    `a person who is not the child's parent`

-- "the terms 'father', 'mother' and 'parent' shall be construed accordingly" (s 65, line
-- 807): a person who stands to the child as above is its father or its mother.
DECLARE `Father or mother` IS ONE OF
    `the child's father`
    `the child's mother`

§§ `A parent named in a child's record`

-- `name of the person`: a `name` among the family's persons.
-- `the child is with this person`: s 67(b) "נמצא עם" (is with). A fact about the child's
-- living arrangement on the day.
-- `support proven`: for `a person who is not the child's parent` only, whether it has been
-- proven, to the satisfaction of whoever the Administration authorised, that in the period
-- set in regulations the insured supported the child (s 65 "ילד" (2)). The regulations
-- (line 808) are not in this row's sources; the proof is the authorised person's
-- determination, which a register records. Ignored for every other standing.
-- src:807 | ובלבד שהילד נמצא בישראל ולא מלאו לו 18 שנים; והמונחים ”אב“, ”אם“ ו”הורה“ יתפרשו בהתאם לכך.
-- src:818 | (ב) ילד שיש לו שני הורים, יבוא במנין האב המבוטח זולת אם הוא נמצא עם האם בלבד; ילד שיש לו הורה טבעי והורה אחר והם מבוטחים, יבוא במנין ילדי אותו הורה אשר עמו הוא נמצא.
DECLARE `A parent in a child's record` HAS
    `name of the person`                IS A STRING
    `standing`                          IS A `Standing to the child`
    `father or mother`                  IS A `Father or mother`
    `the child is with this person`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `support proven`                    IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `A child`

-- `married`: s 1 "ילד" excludes a married boy or girl (fork F1).
-- `absence from Israel`: the absence in progress on the day, if any (NOTHING when the child
-- is in Israel). s 65(b) measures it as a period from the day the child left.
-- `the Institute regards the child as in Israel`: the Institute's decision under the second
-- half of s 65(b), for an absence of more than three months. A recorded determination.
-- src:809 | (ב) לא יראו ילד כנמצא בחוץ לארץ אם יצא מישראל לתקופה שאינה עולה על שלושה חודשים; אולם המוסד רשאי לראותו כאילו הוא בישראל גם אם יצא מישראל לתקופה העולה על שלושה חודשים.
DECLARE `An absence from Israel` HAS
    `the day the child left Israel`        IS A DATE
    `the day the child returned to Israel` IS A MAYBE DATE

DECLARE `A child` HAS
    `name`                                           IS A STRING
    `date of birth`                                  IS A DATE
    `married`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `absence from Israel`                            IS A MAYBE `An absence from Israel`
    `the Institute regards the child as in Israel`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `parents`                                        IS A LIST OF `A parent in a child's record`

§§ `A family on a day`

-- The case. `the persons` and `the children` must include every person and child whose
-- counts touch one another: a parent's count is made of all the children s 67 places with
-- that parent, wherever they live.
DECLARE `A family on a day` HAS
    `the day`          IS A DATE
    `the persons`      IS A LIST OF `A person`
    `the children`     IS A LIST OF `A child`

§§ `The basic amounts for the child allowance`

-- The three amounts of s 1 "הסכום הבסיסי" paragraph (2), as in force on the day. Positional
-- `OF` construction is used for this record only in the table of published figures, under a
-- ruler naming the three columns.
-- src:186 | (2) לעניין קצבת הילדים המשתלמת לפי הוראות סימן ב׳ בפרק ד׳, כמפורט להלן:
-- src:187 | (א) בעד הילד הראשון והחמישי ואילך במניין ילדיו של ההורה – 150 שקלים חדשים [note: (נקוב לשנת 2015; בשנים 2024–2025, 169 ש״ח; בשנת 2026, 173 ש״ח)];
-- src:188 | (ב) בעד הילד השני, השלישי והרביעי שבמניין ילדיו של ההורה – 188 שקלים חדשים [note: (נקוב לשנת 2015; בשנים 2024–2025, 214 ש״ח; בשנת 2026, 219 ש״ח)];
-- src:189 | (ג) על אף האמור בפסקאות משנה (א) ו־(ב), לעניין גמלה לפי חוק הבטחת הכנסה, או תוספת כאמור בסעיף 68(ג) – 140 שקלים חדשים [note: (נקוב לשנת 2015; בשנים 2024–2025, 158 ש״ח; בשנת 2026, 162 ש״ח)];
DECLARE `The basic amounts for the child allowance` HAS
    `under paragraph (2)(a)`  IS A NUMBER
    `under paragraph (2)(b)`  IS A NUMBER
    `under paragraph (2)(c)`  IS A NUMBER

§§ `Answers`

-- Which provision fixes the allowance for a child at a place in the count.
DECLARE `The provision that fixes the allowance for a child` IS ONE OF
    `section 68(a), at the basic amount in paragraph (2)(a) of section 1`
    `section 68(a), at the basic amount in paragraph (2)(b) of section 1`
    `section 68(b)(2), a fourth child born before 1 June 2003`
    `section 68(b)(3), a fifth or later child born before 1 June 2003`

-- One line of a parent's allowance. Amounts are monthly and BEFORE ROUNDING: s 381 leaves
-- rounding to rules the Minister makes, which are not in this row's sources.
-- `the supplement under section 68(c), before rounding` is 0 for a child at a place other
-- than third or fourth, or where s 68(c) does not apply: nothing is added.
DECLARE `The allowance for a child in the count` HAS
    `name of the child`                                        IS A STRING
    `place in the count`                                       IS A NUMBER
    `the provision`                                            IS A `The provision that fixes the allowance for a child`
    `the allowance under section 68(a) or (b), before rounding` IS A NUMBER
    `the supplement under section 68(c), before rounding`      IS A NUMBER

-- The answer for one person. The two ways s 66 names for a person to have no allowance are
-- members of the type, not NOTHING (drafting-patterns, "Total enum over MAYBE").
DECLARE `The child allowance of a person for the month` IS ONE OF
    `no child allowance, not being an insured parent`
    `no child allowance, being an insured parent with income chargeable to additional tax`
    `a monthly child allowance` HAS
        `for each child in the count` IS A LIST OF `The allowance for a child in the count`

DECLARE `A person's child allowance for the month` HAS
    `name of the person`   IS A STRING
    `the answer`           IS A `The child allowance of a person for the month`

-- Facts that cannot describe a case: the caller can fix them and ask again (phrasebook 11.4).
DECLARE `A problem with the facts` IS ONE OF
    `two persons have the same name`
    `a child's record names a parent who is not among the persons`
    `two children have the same name`
    `a child is born after the day`
    `an absence from Israel begins after the day, or ends before it begins`
